  "natspec": {
    "functions": {
      "0x313ce567": {
        "notice": "The wrapper decimals, mirroring the underlying token (replaces the base 18)."
      },
      "0x2f4f21e2": {
        "notice": "Deposit `value` underlying tokens from the caller and mint the same number of wrapped tokens to `account`."
      },
      "0x6f307dc3": {
        "notice": "The address of the underlying ERC-20 token being wrapped."
      },
      "0x205c2878": {
        "notice": "Burn `value` wrapped tokens from the caller and send the same number of underlying tokens to `account`."
      }
    },
    "notice": "Stateless Diamond facet — wraps an underlying ERC-20 1:1. Pure delegator to {ERC20WrapperLib}.",
    "dev": "`recover()` is intentionally NOT exposed here: exposing it requires access control, so a deriving facet adds it. `decimals()` overrides the base 18 to mirror the underlying. CUSTODY: the internal `recover` mints the diamond's WHOLE underlying balance above total supply, so a facet that exposes it also mints any other module's escrow of the underlying (an ERC-4626 vault, VestingWallet, BridgeERC20 or ShieldedPool). One custodian per asset per diamond (issue #240)."
  },
